WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.060 --> 00:00:05.180
The Disney Princess team-up in the Wreck-It
Ralph sequel almost broke the internet when

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:07.029
the scene was teased in a trailer.

00:00:07.029 --> 00:00:11.420
And, having watched the movie, I can confirm
that seeing the iconic princesses assemble

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:13.990
for the first time will not disappoint fans!

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:18.820
Yippee-ki-yay, movie lovers, it's Jan here
and today I'm revealing every amazing Disney

00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:23.640
princess detail, secret and easter egg you
need to look out for in Ralph Breaks The Internet.

00:00:23.640 --> 00:00:27.929
Plus keep watching to the end where I'll reveal
some bonus Frozen easter eggs in the movie.

00:00:27.929 --> 00:00:31.900
And to celebrate the the new film, I'm giving
away some awesome Funko Pops.

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:36.270
Hit the bell and make sure you're a subscriber
and leave a comment about the movie to enter.

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:41.070
A really fun moment in Wreck-It Ralph 2 is
when the princesses are so fascinated with

00:00:41.070 --> 00:00:43.960
Vanellope's casual clothes that they want
their own.

00:00:43.960 --> 00:00:47.910
So, Cinderella has her mice make brand new
outfits for everyone.

00:00:47.910 --> 00:00:53.770
And after a 1960s Batman-style transition,
we see the princesses in their new comfy clothing

00:00:53.770 --> 00:00:57.790
and Cinderella sighs, 'ah, so this is love'.

00:00:57.790 --> 00:01:01.670
Cinders' words poke fun at the song she sings
when she dances with Prince Charming at the

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:06.159
ball and also mock the Disney princess cliché
of true love.

00:01:06.159 --> 00:01:10.149
While each piece of the princesses' new clothing
matches the colour scheme of their iconic

00:01:10.149 --> 00:01:14.619
outfits, what's especially interesting is
that they're also loaded with easter eggs

00:01:14.619 --> 00:01:15.749
and inside jokes.

00:01:15.749 --> 00:01:20.490
The tank top Rapunzel wears under her hoodie
has a design which reads "We gotta dream,

00:01:20.490 --> 00:01:24.940
the Snuggly Ducklings", a clever call-back
to the song in Tangled "I've Got A Dream"

00:01:24.940 --> 00:01:28.609
which Rapunzel sang with the regulars at the
rowdy pub "The Snuggly Duckling".

00:01:28.609 --> 00:01:33.139
Her leggings also have a pattern with the
sun crest symbol of Rapunzel's kingdom of

00:01:33.139 --> 00:01:34.139
Corona.

00:01:34.139 --> 00:01:38.609
For Ariel, the words "gizmos", "whozits",
and "whatzits" appear on her top referring

00:01:38.609 --> 00:01:42.219
to the lyrics of her iconic song "Part of
Your World".

00:01:42.219 --> 00:01:47.229
And in keeping with Ariel's love of all things
human, she's so amazed at her new "thingamabob",

00:01:47.229 --> 00:01:54.469
aka shirt, that she even launches in to song,
singing "I once had a dream that I might wear

00:01:54.469 --> 00:01:55.469
a shirt".

00:01:55.469 --> 00:01:59.369
Pocahontas's sweater has a design of a wolf
howling at the moon plus the words "Blue Corn

00:01:59.369 --> 00:02:03.930
Moon" in a nod to that same line in her song
"Colors of the Wind".

00:02:03.930 --> 00:02:08.310
Cinderella's jumper has an image of her classic
pumpkin carriage plus "G2G", aka "Got To Go",

00:02:08.310 --> 00:02:12.879
a fun throwback to how she had to leave the
ball before midnight.

00:02:12.879 --> 00:02:17.450
And, look at the bean bag she's sitting on,
it's patterned with sparkles like the ones

00:02:17.450 --> 00:02:22.450
from the Fairy Godmother's magic wand during
Cinderella's transformation scene.

00:02:22.450 --> 00:02:26.460
Belle has a silhouette in the shape of the
Beast on her shirt with the letters "BFF"

00:02:26.460 --> 00:02:29.640
which, in this case, are short for "Beast
Friends Forever".

00:02:29.640 --> 00:02:34.250
Anna's shirt has a "we finish each other's
sandwiches" theme in a shout-out to her song

00:02:34.250 --> 00:02:36.689
with Hans, "Love Is An Open Door".

00:02:36.689 --> 00:02:41.209
And Elsa has a blue and white coloured "Just
Let It Go" sweater referencing her iconic

00:02:41.209 --> 00:02:42.209
song.

00:02:42.209 --> 00:02:46.629
The "NOLA" on Tiana's top is short for "New
Orleans, Louisiana" where she's from and the

00:02:46.629 --> 00:02:50.250
crown in the middle of the "O" reflects the
design of The Princess and the Frog's title

00:02:50.250 --> 00:02:53.830
card and is also a hat-tip to Prince Naveen.

00:02:53.830 --> 00:02:58.140
Moana has hashtag "Shiny" on her shirt together
with a picture of Tamatoa, the villainous

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:01.590
giant crab who sang the memorable song "Shiny"
in her movie.

00:03:01.590 --> 00:03:06.439
Mulan wears a bomber jacket that sports some
Mushu artwork on the front and back in honour

00:03:06.439 --> 00:03:08.689
of her dragon companion and friend.

00:03:08.689 --> 00:03:13.691
Snow White gets a poison apple-themed top,
Jasmine has the genie's three wishes, and

00:03:13.691 --> 00:03:17.829
Sleeping Beauty's top appropriately points
out that she's the "Nap Queen".

00:03:17.829 --> 00:03:21.861
Merida's shirt has a bear and the word "mum"
on the front because her mother [Queen Elinor]

00:03:21.861 --> 00:03:24.570
transformed into a bear after eating enchanted
cake.

00:03:24.570 --> 00:03:29.020
There are also tons of amazing background
details and easter eggs for fans to uncover

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:33.609
in the scene, especially on the princesses'
individual dressing tables.

00:03:33.609 --> 00:03:37.209
For example, Belle often switches back to
reading during the scene and so, of course,

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:38.870
there's a stack of books in her cubicle.

00:03:38.870 --> 00:03:43.170
Just in front of the books on the table, is
the magic mirror from Beauty and the Beast,

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.400
and a candelabra, which is a hat-tip to Lumiere.

00:03:45.400 --> 00:03:50.489
In Ariel's cubicle, there's a reminder of
her fascination with human objects because

00:03:50.489 --> 00:03:54.150
if you look very carefully, you'll spot a
box of thingamabobs.

00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:57.590
And you can also see the candelabra from her
secret grotto.

00:03:57.590 --> 00:04:01.620
On Tiana's mirror, there's a picture of "Tiana's
Place", the restaurant she and her father

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:06.310
dreamed of opening and which became a reality
for her in The Princess And The Frog, and

00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:10.790
on the table, there's a plate of her famous
"man-catching" beignets.

00:04:10.790 --> 00:04:14.780
Also in the background is a photograph of
young Tiana with her parents.

00:04:14.780 --> 00:04:20.299
Continuing the bear theme of Merida's clothes,
she has several toy bears on her vanity table.

00:04:20.299 --> 00:04:24.669
On top of Anna's dressing table, you can see
a vase of sunflowers, which reflects just

00:04:24.669 --> 00:04:29.270
how much she loves those flowers as we've
seen throughout the Frozen films.

00:04:29.270 --> 00:04:33.190
And you can also just about make out the dolls
of the sisters which appeared during the "Do

00:04:33.190 --> 00:04:34.190
You Wanna Build A Snowman?"

00:04:34.190 --> 00:04:36.900
song in the first Frozen movie.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:42.150
In Rapunzel's area, you can see her chameleon
Pascal sitting on top of her paint box, and

00:04:42.150 --> 00:04:46.639
there's a painting of an owl, which is a shout-out
to the owl belonging to her friend and handmaiden

00:04:46.639 --> 00:04:50.250
Cassandra in the Tangled TV series.

00:04:50.250 --> 00:04:54.440
Cinderella has a pumpkin on her dresser as
well as a clock that's stuck at midnight and

00:04:54.440 --> 00:04:58.620
Jasmine, of course, has Aladdin's magic carpet
and the genie's lamp.

00:04:58.620 --> 00:05:02.830
The crests above each dressing area are also
suitable symbols for each princess.

00:05:02.830 --> 00:05:07.750
For Ariel, there's a nautilus shell referencing
Ursula's enchanted necklace which held Ariel's

00:05:07.750 --> 00:05:11.830
voice that she gave to the sea witch in exchange
for human legs.

00:05:11.830 --> 00:05:16.919
Tiana has a water lily, Rapunzel has the magical
golden flower, the Frozen sisters have a crocus

00:05:16.919 --> 00:05:21.000
reminiscent of the official crest of Arendelle,
and Cinderella has a glass slipper.

00:05:21.000 --> 00:05:25.780
There are also some clever little tributes
and easter eggs to signature details we associate

00:05:25.780 --> 00:05:27.150
with the princesses.

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:31.930
As Vanellope glitches into the room, Aurora
is asleep on a chaise longue holding a red

00:05:31.930 --> 00:05:36.539
rose and in exactly the same pose she was
during her enchanted slumber in her original

00:05:36.539 --> 00:05:38.430
1959 movie.

00:05:38.430 --> 00:05:42.819
Rapunzel continues to indulge her love of
painting as you can spot her here very briefly

00:05:42.819 --> 00:05:45.729
painting on the side walls of her dressing
area!

00:05:45.729 --> 00:05:49.930
And while the other princesses lounge around
on chairs, bean bags or cushions, Rapunzel

00:05:49.930 --> 00:05:53.130
actually sits in a chair of her own hair!

00:05:53.130 --> 00:05:58.160
Another detail you'll need to look carefully
for is Cinderella plucking a leaf out of Pocahontas's

00:05:58.160 --> 00:05:59.160
hair.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:03.000
That moment is a little homage to the leaves
we see swirling around Pocahontas during her

00:06:03.000 --> 00:06:04.849
song "Colors of the Wind".

00:06:04.849 --> 00:06:08.900
And in another nod to that song, watch how
Pocahontas's hair is constantly in motion

00:06:08.900 --> 00:06:13.560
with magical wind blowing through her tresses
even though she's indoors.

00:06:13.560 --> 00:06:17.710
And when the princesses spring into action
they brandish many of their signature weapons

00:06:17.710 --> 00:06:22.550
or items, with Cinderella going hilariously
dark and smashing her glass slipper making

00:06:22.550 --> 00:06:23.840
it into a shiv.

00:06:23.840 --> 00:06:28.419
You'll have doubtless noticed Merida's bow,
Mulan's sword, Belle's book and Rapunzel's

00:06:28.419 --> 00:06:32.900
frying pan, but a little harder to spot is
Ariel brandishing her dinglehopper.

00:06:32.900 --> 00:06:34.009
"What is it?"

00:06:34.009 --> 00:06:36.349
"It's a dinglehopper."

00:06:36.349 --> 00:06:41.160
Also in this shot, Elsa stands ready to ice
Vanellope with her freezing powers.

00:06:41.160 --> 00:06:45.500
Elsa's sister Anna doesn't have a weapon,
but she does have her fists at the ready,

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:49.449
which is a nice call-back to that moment in
Frozen where she punched the villainous Hans

00:06:49.449 --> 00:06:51.509
in the face.

00:06:51.509 --> 00:06:55.650
Moana has the oar we've seen her use to threaten
Maui.

00:06:55.650 --> 00:06:58.849
Tiana, being the gifted cook she is, has a
rolling pin.

00:06:58.849 --> 00:07:01.909
And Sleeping Beauty has a spindle from her
spinning wheel.

00:07:01.909 --> 00:07:06.509
Pocahontas wields the club that her father
was going to use to execute John Smith.

00:07:06.509 --> 00:07:08.990
And Jasmine brandishes the Genie's lamp.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:13.610
There's also a cameo appearance by Pocahontas's
raccoon Meeko although he's clearly not a

00:07:13.610 --> 00:07:18.590
fan of Vanellope when she goes to pet him;
and we also see Cinderella with her mice and

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:21.110
birds, and Jasmine with her pet tiger Rahjah.

00:07:21.110 --> 00:07:26.229
There's another funny nod to Aurora's sleepiness
when she starts to doze off while Merida's

00:07:26.229 --> 00:07:27.229
talking.

00:07:27.229 --> 00:07:31.879
Merida wakes her up with a jolt and the look
on Aurora's face is just priceless.

00:07:31.879 --> 00:07:36.780
Near the start of the scene, after Pocahontas
asks Vanellope what type of princess she is,

00:07:36.780 --> 00:07:40.199
the other princesses humorously run through
a list of tropes that have been part of their

00:07:40.199 --> 00:07:41.720
characters over the years.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:43.180
"Do you have magic hair?"

00:07:43.180 --> 00:07:44.180
"No."

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:45.180
"Magic hands?"

00:07:45.180 --> 00:07:46.180
"No."

00:07:46.180 --> 00:07:47.180
"Do animals talk to you?"

00:07:47.180 --> 00:07:48.180
"No."

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.180
"Were you poisoned?"

00:07:49.180 --> 00:07:50.180
"No."

00:07:50.180 --> 00:07:51.330
"Cursed, kidnapped or enslaved?"

00:07:51.330 --> 00:07:52.330
"No!

00:07:52.330 --> 00:07:53.330
Are you guys OK?

00:07:53.330 --> 00:07:54.330
Shall I call the police?"

00:07:54.330 --> 00:07:56.909
"Then I have to assume you made a deal with
an underwater sea witch where she took your

00:07:56.909 --> 00:08:00.550
voice in exchange for a pair of human legs!"

00:08:00.550 --> 00:08:01.550
"No.

00:08:01.550 --> 00:08:02.550
Good lord!

00:08:02.550 --> 00:08:04.300
Who would do that?!"

00:08:04.300 --> 00:08:05.300
"Have you ever had true love's kiss?"

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:06.300
"Eugh!

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:07.300
Barf!"

00:08:07.300 --> 00:08:08.300
"Do you have daddy issues?"

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:09.300
"I don't even have a mom."

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:10.300
"Neither do we!"

00:08:10.300 --> 00:08:13.409
That last joke is a reference to the dark
truth that so many Disney princesses don't

00:08:13.409 --> 00:08:15.610
actually have a mother who's still alive.

00:08:15.610 --> 00:08:19.639
Which is possibly due to the fact that Walt
Disney felt responsible for the death of his

00:08:19.639 --> 00:08:24.250
own mother, so the theory is the studio adopted
a kind of "no mothers" policy in the stories

00:08:24.250 --> 00:08:25.250
they developed.

00:08:25.250 --> 00:08:29.849
Now, if the princess scenes in Ralph Breaks
The Internet impressed you with how true they

00:08:29.849 --> 00:08:33.860
felt to the original characters, that's in
part because most of the original actors who

00:08:33.860 --> 00:08:37.390
voiced the characters returned to record lines
for the new movie.

00:08:37.390 --> 00:08:41.279
In fact, when each actress came in to the
studio to record her lines, she would often

00:08:41.279 --> 00:08:45.060
make some little tweaks and changes to make
the script feel slightly more authentic to

00:08:45.060 --> 00:08:46.430
each princess.

00:08:46.430 --> 00:08:49.410
Of course, some of the original actresses
weren't available.

00:08:49.410 --> 00:08:54.140
Adriana Caselotti, who voiced Snow White,
and Ilene Woods, who voiced Cinderella, are

00:08:54.140 --> 00:08:58.560
sadly no longer with us and Mary Costa, the
original voice of Aurora, is retired.

00:08:58.560 --> 00:09:03.880
However, Jennifer Hale and Kate Higgins provided
voices for Cinderella and Aurora respectively

00:09:03.880 --> 00:09:07.280
as they have voiced those characters in recent
Disney projects.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:11.660
And lending her voice to Snow White was Ralph
Breaks The Internet co-writer Pamela Ribon.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:16.310
There are also some other great Disney princess
easter eggs peppered throughout the film.

00:09:16.310 --> 00:09:20.620
During the pancake-milkshake game, the little
toddler watching looks incredibly like baby

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:21.620
Moana.

00:09:21.620 --> 00:09:25.240
It seems a deliberate choice by the filmmakers
as the little girl's official name has been

00:09:25.240 --> 00:09:26.829
revealed as "Mo".

00:09:26.829 --> 00:09:30.649
On top of that, there's an even sneakier easter
egg in this scene because Mo's mother, who's

00:09:30.649 --> 00:09:35.510
driving the car, is actually voiced by Nicole
Scherzinger, who also voiced Moana's mother

00:09:35.510 --> 00:09:38.290
in the 2016 animated movie.

00:09:38.290 --> 00:09:43.200
I also noticed several other Frozen easter
eggs outside the main princess scenes in Ralph

00:09:43.200 --> 00:09:44.200
Breaks The Internet.

00:09:44.200 --> 00:09:49.500
When Vanellope arrives at Oh My Disney, listen
out for the pop version of Frozen's "Let It

00:09:49.500 --> 00:09:50.500
Go".

00:09:50.500 --> 00:09:54.340
And among the viral cat videos that Ralph
and Vanellope encounter is one of a grumpy-looking

00:09:54.340 --> 00:09:57.279
cat pushing a little Anna doll off a table.

00:09:57.279 --> 00:10:01.640
Also, the Frozen sisters' father King Agnarr
appears in a pop-up ad!

00:10:01.640 --> 00:10:05.770
Finally, there's an amazing additional scene
with the princesses late on in Ralph Breaks

00:10:05.770 --> 00:10:10.290
The Internet, however, I don't want to spoil
it here so I may do a separate video about

00:10:10.290 --> 00:10:11.290
that.

00:10:11.290 --> 00:10:13.640
Now, who's your favourite Disney princess
in the movie?

00:10:13.640 --> 00:10:17.550
And would you like to see any of the princesses
team up for their own film?

00:10:17.550 --> 00:10:21.709
Don't forget to comment and subscribe for
a chance to win a Funko Pop.

00:10:21.709 --> 00:10:25.800
Tap left for my next Wreck-It Ralph video
or tap right for another video you're sure

00:10:25.800 --> 00:10:26.800
to like!

00:10:26.800 --> 00:10:30.380
And if you enjoyed this, remember to share
and leave a thumbs-up for more videos like

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:31.380
this.

00:10:31.380 --> 00:10:33.160
Thanks for watching and see ya next time.

